  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm temperatures and breezy winds Sunday \nbefore the next rain chances early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure builds over the region Saturday and moves off the\ncoast to our south Sunday. Breezy winds out of the southwest \nwill develop between the high and the weakened remnants of \nHurricane Isaias as it moves into the Ohio valley Saturday night\ninto Sunday. These winds will help to funnel warmer \ntemperatures (upper 60s) into the area for Sunday and Monday, \npotentially 10 degrees above average for this time of year. As \nthe system moves off the southern New England coast, it could \nbring a chance of showers for the Downeast coast Sunday night \ninto Monday. Rain chances could decrease if the system stays \nfurther south, though there is still a good amount of \nuncertainty at this time. A separate low pressure develops over \nthe Great Lakes Monday night as a trough deepens behind the \ndeparting tropical remnants. This will bring a chance of rain \nearly mid next week.",
